{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And He brought him outside.</b> According to its plain sense, He brought him outside his tent to see the stars. And according to its midrash — He said to him: Go out of your astrology, which you have seen in the constellations, that you are not destined to raise a son: Abram has no son, but Abraham has a son; Sarai does not give birth, but Sarah gives birth — I call you by another name and the constellation changes. Another interpretation: He brought him outside the space of the world and raised him above the stars, and this is the sense of הַבָּטָה — looking from above downward."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:43.074193202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}